        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. Having regard to the rival submissions made by both the learned counsel and having gone through the material available on record, to quash the proceedings under Section 482 of Cr.P.C, the Court has to see whether the averments in the com"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d547a38e74324801bc058272b5040b9f_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. At this stage, it is pertinent to note the Judgment of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in State of Madhya Pradesh vs. SKS,J Surendra Kori 1, wherein in paragraph No.14 it is held as follows:\n\"The High Court in exercise of its powers under Sect"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "93d64d1bc9b74973bee71e859b3eaf61_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "This Court has, in several judgments, held that the inherent jurisdiction under Section 482 Cr.P.C., though wide, has to be used sparingly, carefully and with caution."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "577704573924461cbec70917140d64f9_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The High Court, under Section 482 Cr.P.C.,\nshould normally refrain from giving a prima facie decision in a case where the entire facts are incomplete and hazy, more so when the evidence has not been collected and produced before the Court a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f75e6d7f1d664396bad37e951f0b8e11_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As seen from the record, the allegations against the petitioners are that they prepared egg fried rice and the same was unhygienic, due to which, 36 students got vomited."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f6a3471b8d854bfe8c3398871fe468f3_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Perusal of FSL report reveals that there is no poisonous substance in the food and the RIMS, Adilabad report reveals that Klebsiella Pneumonia was found in the samples and the same can be associated with diarrhea like illness."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "71d2170a49f841f3b032a53c9558ee69_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But, proper hand hygiene and washing of vegetables before preparing food can prevent the illness."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0827ea5c12b245cda0b52fa28f21fcbc_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Whether the non-hygenic condition is (2012) 10 Supreme Court Cases 155 SKS,J not a proper explanation and the report given by RIMS is not proper, whether the said bacteria is harmful Veeramaneni Jithendher vs The State Of Telangana on 8 Apr"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "63010dc775b64dfa82879983d3968205_32",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "11. In view of the above discussion as well as the law laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in State of Madhya Pradesh (supra), this Court does not find any merit in the criminal petition to quash the proceedings against the petitioner an"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "27a43cdb988942bbb1556ae43002ebee_33",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12. Accordingly, the criminal petition is dismissed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bf4f13f1003f4e5798ac00b8ccb63a32_34",
